  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The Fanuc post (`assets/posts/fanuc.cps`) has a new option, \"Manual Guide i blank (G1902 / G1900)\" (`manualGuideBlank`). The default is off.\n- With the option on, the post writes one blank block for each program. The block comes after `G21` / `G20` and before the first `G90 G54` and `T.. M6`.\n  - A box stock gives `G1902 B D H I J K`. Example: a 100 x 60 x 30 block with G54 at the top centre gives `G1902 B100. D60. H30. I50. J30. K30.`\n  - A round bar along Z with its axis on the work origin gives `G1900 D L K`. K is `StockZTop - OriginZ`, the distance from the work origin to the positive-Z end face (Fanuc B-63874EN/05, printed page 193, PDF page 215). A diameter 60, length 30 bar with a top-face origin gives `G1900 D60. L30. K0.`. An origin below the top face gives positive K. A negative K produces a refusal comment instead of a blank block.\n  - Each other stock gives the comment `(NO BLANK BLOCK - <reason>)` and no block.\n- The app stream has three new PARAMs after `StockZTop`: `StockShape`, `StockShapeBottom` and `StockShapeDiameter` (a bar only). A new module writes them: `crates/app/src/posting_stock_shape.rs`. `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md` has the new row.\n- The Heidenhain Klartext post refuses each PARAM that is not on its positive list. It now ignores the three new PARAMs. Its output does not change. Without this change, `klartext_builtin` failed with \"unsupported parameter StockShape\".\n- A tester kit for the Robodrill is in `docs/tester-kits/fanuc-mgi-blank/`. A test pins it to the post output, byte for byte.\n- The decision record is `docs/decisions/2769-mgi-blank.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThis is a new feature. The research comment on #2769 gives the addresses. The stream did not tell a box from a bar or from a model stock. The stream also did not state the stock bottom for a mill without a controller identity.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `crates/post/tests/fanuc_mgi_blank.rs` (12 tests):\n  - `off_by_default_no_blank_and_no_comment`\n  - `a_box_posts_g1902_before_the_first_g90_and_tool_change`\n  - `a_box_with_an_offset_origin_posts_signed_distances`\n  - `an_inch_program_writes_the_blank_in_inch`\n  - `a_z_bar_on_the_origin_posts_g1900`\n  - `a_z_bar_with_the_origin_below_its_top_posts_the_end_face_distance`\n  - `a_z_bar_requiring_negative_k_posts_a_comment`\n  - `a_z_bar_off_the_origin_posts_a_comment`\n  - `a_z_bar_without_its_diameter_posts_a_comment`\n  - `a_stock_no_block_describes_posts_a_comment_not_a_block` (10 reasons)\n  - `two_operations_write_one_blank`\n  - `the_tester_kit_is_what_the_post_writes`\n- `crates/app/tests/stock_shape_stream.rs` (3 tests): `a_box_stock_states_box_and_its_bottom`, `a_cylinder_states_its_axis_and_diameter`, `a_stock_off_the_world_axes_states_rotated`.\n- Red before the fix:\n  - With the upstream `fanuc.cps`, 8 of the first 9 post pins fail. Only the off-by-default pin passes, as it must.\n  - With the upstream `posting.rs`, the 3 app pins fail.\n- Mutations (each one red, then green after the restore):\n  - Restored the old lower-end K expression: `a_z_bar_on_the_origin_posts_g1900`, `a_z_bar_with_the_origin_below_its_top_posts_the_end_face_distance`, and `the_tester_kit_is_what_the_post_writes` fail (9 passed, 3 failed). Restore: 12 passed.\n  - Removed the negative-K guard: `a_z_bar_requiring_negative_k_posts_a_comment` fails. Restore: 12 passed.\n  - No WCS yaw guard: `a_stock_no_block_describes_posts_a_comment_not_a_block` fails.\n  - No bar-centre guard: `a_z_bar_off_the_origin_posts_a_comment` fails.\n  - No \"once\" guard: `two_operations_write_one_blank` fails.\n  - App: a turned box read as `box`: `a_stock_off_the_world_axes_states_rotated` fails.\n- Corrected-head validation: `2629421fd40513c62feed899525cf8ac01622331`: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed (338 steps, 0 failed, 24.1 minutes; post: 47 suites / 363 tests passed; app: 289 suites / 2,177 tests passed / 7 ignored). `cargo clippy -j 12 -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed (1m 21s). Worktree clean; `git diff --check` passed.\n- Required heavy lanes: `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` passed on the corrected head (204 steps, 0 failed gate steps, 34.7 minutes). The reached lane was **app heavy: every target**: the release `--no-run` build and all 203 app steps ran. This includes `lib`, `bins`, `doc`, `rotary_field_parity` (6 passed), `shared_face_bodies_finish` (6 passed), `stock_field_cost`, `stock_play_precalc`, and `whole_model_pocket`. The 201 successful suite summaries report 46 passed tests. Two additional expected-red checks matched their recorded failures and were accepted by the gate: `app heavy: known fail #1950 the_users_whole_model_bore_roughs_adaptive_on_each_level` and `app heavy: known fail #2849 fig8_outside_containment_with_em0800_and_clearing_kinds_works`. These are known failures, not passing tests. No heavy steps were skipped.\n- The first gate run found `klartext_builtin` red (the Klartext positive list). The Klartext change above fixes it. The test is green in the final run.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The option is off by default. The new PARAMs are not read by any post when the option is off.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real control. The bar K definition follows the manual end-face diagram. The kit remains for graphic-simulation verification on a control.\n- Manual Guide i reads the blank in the control's input unit. An inch program on a metric control is not checked.\n- `G1906` (a bar along X) is not written. It posts a comment. The research comment plans it after the kit test.\n- An end-to-end in-app post with the option on (app world to Fanuc text) is not tested. The two halves are tested: the app stream PARAMs and the post on a recorded stream.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- PR #3280 changes `assets/posts/fanuc.cps` (`declaredOptions`, `startPreamble`, `endPreamble`, `onCycle`). This PR changes `declaredOptions` at a different line, `onSection`, and adds a new function. The functions that change are different. The PR that merges second refreshes.\n- Many open PRs change `crates/app/src/posting.rs` (for example #2951, #2955, #2964, #2968, #2969, #2972). This PR adds two lines in `op_streams_by` after `edm_params::insert`, and one module declaration. The PR that merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Fanuc post: the new option \"Manual Guide i blank (G1902 / G1900)\" writes the setup's stock as a Manual Guide i blank block for the graphic simulation (off by default).\n\nFixes #2769\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
